  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "From ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "70121:9d0151bf-07d5-422a-a841-600a0d11b53d",
        "localId": "65c5a41f-a533-4285-8397-ab77f6adc4f5",
        "text": "@Illtud Daniel"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": " during the OCFL discussion at Virtual Showcase 2025:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Q re ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://ocfl.github.io/extensions/0008-schema-registry.html"
         },
         "type": "link"
        },
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": "extension 0008",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": ", schema registry. What's the status of extensions and any chance this will be included in 2?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Does Fedora have any plans to support this?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Illtud used the recent LoC showdown as an example of when this would be useful (schema access disappearing and tooling is unable to validate against external schema). Also in terms of OCFL’s goal of being self-describing, this furthers the case by embedding the schemas that describe the objects held within. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
